 ],
 "_reuse_note": {
  "Key of Terror/Hate/Destruction": "All 3 share ONE sprite in-game (misc.txt: all three code pk1/pk2/pk3 use invfile=invmph -> mephisto_key.sprite). Not a shortcut -- this is exactly how D2R renders them; they are visually identical, distinguished only by tooltip name.",
  "Bone Break/Black Cleft/Crack of the Heavens/Cold Rupture/Flame Rift/Rotting Fissure": "RotW-mod Sunder Charms have base type Grand Charm. D2R has no per-unique-charm sprite (same as vanilla LoD unique small/large charms) -- every Grand Charm, unique or not, renders with the single generic Grand Charm icon. Mapped to the existing art/hd_charm_large.png (already CASC-extracted, base 'Charm, Large'). Not fabricated -- same inheritance principle already used for elite/exceptional base items reusing their normal base's invfile sprite."
 },
 "_known_gaps_no_casc_equivalent": {
  "Worldstone Shard (Western/Eastern/Southern/Northern/Deep)": "RotW-mod-exclusive item name. Searched full CASC enumeration (175,827 files) for 'worldstone'/'shard' under items/misc -- no matching sprite exists in the vanilla Battle.net D2R install. These are mod-fabricated items with no real in-game art to extract. Left on existing diablo2.io fallback art (art/western_graphic.png etc) -- do NOT fabricate a sprite for these.",
  "Colossal Ancient Jewels (Bile/Thunder/Frost/Fire/Stone/Light)": "Also RotW-mod-exclusive (not in MATERIAL_CATS/Materials tab, but flagged during this audit). No 'jewel'-named CASC item sprite beyond the generic base Jewel. Not pulled this pass -- flag for a future session if Konyo wants the base Jewel icon (art/hd_jewel.png, if extracted) applied here."
 },
